{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/942061-your-experiences-running-boston-unveiled","id":942061,"title":"Your experiences running Boston Unveiled?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-02T10:33:51-07:00","id":942061,"title":"Your experiences running Boston Unveiled?","content":"I ask this because most people seem to see the Nemean as a plot device, the typical moustache\u00b4d villain waiting to be taken down by the PCs, however I recently ran a chronicle where he actually turned out to be the &quot;good&quot; guy(he is still a douche to people, but he works behind the scenes to stop the Prince of 100.000 leaves) and the Brotherhood of the Ineffable(?) Truth turned out to be a powerhungry and warmonger cabal, eventually falling under the influence of the Prince. I tried to present the Nemean as a tragic figure, someone who holds a secret so horrible that it has weighed on him heavily over the years, molding him into an old resentful men.<br /> <br /> I did this mostly to mess with my PC\u00b4s expectations, I knew they had also read the source material and so I gave them plenty of false red herrings before they finally realized the Noose were actually the &quot;good&quot; guys.<br /> <br /> What are your experience running this awesome scenario?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6378,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6378-br_malk","user":"BR_Malk","date":". 08-02-2016, 01:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6378-br_malk","name":"BR_Malk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T10:48:00-07:00","id":942073,"title":"","content":"Did you use the additional material from the various stories that elaborate on him a bit?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T11:00:42-07:00","id":942084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/942061-your-experiences-running-boston-unveiled?p=942073#post942073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did you use the additional material from the various stories that elaborate on him a bit?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, though obviously I ignored the semi-canon that states that he was actually working *for* the Prince in exchange for a &quot;baronship&quot;(I gave this role to Chain Parris, who had been playing the Nemean for a fool). As I said, I tweaked it to mess with my player's expectations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6378,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6378-br_malk","user":"BR_Malk","date":". 08-02-2016, 03:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6378-br_malk","name":"BR_Malk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T11:38:15-07:00","id":942117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BR_Malk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/942061-your-experiences-running-boston-unveiled#post942061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I ask this because most people seem to see the Nemean as a plot device, the typical moustache\u00b4d villain waiting to be taken down by the PCs, however I recently ran a chronicle where he actually turned out to be the &quot;good&quot; guy(he is still a douche to people, but he works behind the scenes to stop the Prince of 100.000 leaves) and the Brotherhood of the Ineffable(?) Truth turned out to be a powerhungry and warmonger cabal, eventually falling under the influence of the Prince. I tried to present the Nemean as a tragic figure, someone who holds a secret so horrible that it has weighed on him heavily over the years, molding him into an old resentful men.<br /> <br /> I did this mostly to mess with my PC\u00b4s expectations, I knew they had also read the source material and so I gave them plenty of false red herrings before they finally realized the Noose were actually the &quot;good&quot; guys.<br /> <br /> What are your experience running this awesome scenario?</div> </div> </div> </div>My experience was to just remove him and and the witchcraft cabals from my game. I like boston as a setting, both in RL and the way was presented in mage it is an interesting setting. However one of the weakest is the cabals, not the member themselves but the cabals weirdly enough.<br /> <br /> The main issue for me was that we know what fuels and keeps the main conflict to overboard is the secret accord however in typical NWoD fashion the book throws up it hands and makes what the actually entails completely up to the DM, which to me is problematic because whatever the accord turns up to be it will affect the personalities and goals of the 2 main cabals. And as a mistery it only affect the PCs who will give a crap about that and wanna risk it as the last person who investigate was murdered unless one wanna make the Nemean hostigate the players until they have enough and that they decide to follow up with that particular plot instead of just killing him outright in typical PC fashion.<br /> <br /> The main cabals themselves are bloated just to give them superior number agaisnt the PCs, making bunch of their member just forgetabble or not making that much sense. What i find weird though is that now in 2E boston doesnt work as city as mage forge a concilium apparently around a big mistery but openly investigating the secret accord is declaring oneself as a political enemy of the nemean and the rest.<br /> <br /> The NPCs themselves are interesting but the cabals themselves are, to me dull, the 2 main cabals smell to much of ascension. The arrow cabal who is obsese with duel is kinda dull just like the casino robbing and guardian cabals, the members are fine and their locations are interesting but the cabals themselves range from aimless to apolitical to secretive enough that PCs wont interact with them unless the DM force them to it.<br /> <br /> However i find the barest of bones of the main conflict interesting enough that being &quot;2 powerful cabals fighting for dominance with 1 leader figure keeping it barely contained&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T11:58:01-07:00","id":942134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/942061-your-experiences-running-boston-unveiled?p=942117#post942117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What i find weird though is that now in 2E boston doesnt work as city as mage forge a concilium apparently around a big mistery but openly investigating the secret accord is declaring oneself as a political enemy of the nemean and the rest.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't say that. A consilium is set up where there is a density of magi that their conflicts become a problem. Whether it's becuase there's one big mystery or many small ones doesn't matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T12:09:36-07:00","id":942137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/942061-your-experiences-running-boston-unveiled?p=942134#post942134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It doesn't say that. A consilium is set up where there is a density of magi that their conflicts become a problem. Whether it's becuase there's one big mystery or many small ones doesn't matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>But there arent that many &quot;small misteries&quot;, no cabal apparently care about the combat zone and i think the only one left was something about the sea i dont remember or have the book with me now. The tremere asylum is also ignored. Which is weird to me because those 2 are way WAY more interesting than the impenetrable plot of the secret accord.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mage 2E;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wherever many mages gather in a region with a compelling long-term Mystery or many smaller Mysteries, the danger of conflict arises. Cabals dispute control of resources and real estate, to say nothing of access to contested Mysteries.</div> </div> </div> </div>The other problem, aside from interesting characters in boring cabals, is that there isnt much of a dispute for resources. The two main cabals fight over reasons (meaning whatever the DM decides the secret accord works), there is pirate cabal that is just there, there is a crime cabal , dueling cabal and casino stealing cabal that also are just there following no mistery (though i dont remember the crime one if the leader wasnt up to something) there is a powerhungry cabal that does have a defined agenda so does the cabal with the old lady as their leader and a cabal of mysterium obesse with blood purity and atlantis.<br /> .<br /> So the only thing the *could* fight for is places of mana and even then thats pretty meh because all cabals i think already have their places of power designated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T12:19:45-07:00","id":942150,"title":"","content":"The Combat Zone is of interest, but it's also infested with Banishers","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T12:31:43-07:00","id":942155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/942061-your-experiences-running-boston-unveiled?p=942137#post942137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But there arent that many &quot;small misteries&quot;,</div> </div> </div> </div>The book wasn't written with that in mind, but they're there if you want to use the more active 2E setup.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T12:40:17-07:00","id":942161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/942061-your-experiences-running-boston-unveiled?p=942117#post942117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My experience was to just remove him and and the witchcraft cabals from my game. I like boston as a setting, both in RL and the way was presented in mage it is an interesting setting. However one of the weakest is the cabals, not the member themselves but the cabals weirdly enough.<br /> <br /> The main issue for me was that we know what fuels and keeps the main conflict to overboard is the secret accord however in typical NWoD fashion the book throws up it hands and makes what the actually entails completely up to the DM, which to me is problematic because whatever the accord turns up to be it will affect the personalities and goals of the 2 main cabals. And as a mistery it only affect the PCs who will give a crap about that and wanna risk it as the last person who investigate was murdered unless one wanna make the Nemean hostigate the players until they have enough and that they decide to follow up with that particular plot instead of just killing him outright in typical PC fashion.<br /> <br /> The main cabals themselves are bloated just to give them superior number agaisnt the PCs, making bunch of their member just forgetabble or not making that much sense. What i find weird though is that now in 2E boston doesnt work as city as mage forge a concilium apparently around a big mistery but openly investigating the secret accord is declaring oneself as a political enemy of the nemean and the rest.<br /> <br /> The NPCs themselves are interesting but the cabals themselves are, to me dull, the 2 main cabals smell to much of ascension. The arrow cabal who is obsese with duel is kinda dull just like the casino robbing and guardian cabals, the members are fine and their locations are interesting but the cabals themselves range from aimless to apolitical to secretive enough that PCs wont interact with them unless the DM force them to it.<br /> <br /> However i find the barest of bones of the main conflict interesting enough that being &quot;2 powerful cabals fighting for dominance with 1 leader figure keeping it barely contained&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yea, I also got rid of half of the Cabals, I only used those I deemed the most interesting from a RP perspective: The Noose, The Brotherhood, White Putnams, Shadow Chorus, Sanguine Laurel and the Wrens. The others were lesser cabals mostly aligned with the Free Council.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6378-br_malk","name":"BR_Malk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T11:05:28-07:00","id":942818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/942061-your-experiences-running-boston-unveiled?p=942150#post942150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Combat Zone is of interest, but it's also infested with Banishers</div> </div> </div> </div>And yet no cabal cares. The big mayority exist in their own little plot bubble separate from the rest.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BR_Malk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/942061-your-experiences-running-boston-unveiled?p=942161#post942161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yea, I also got rid of half of the Cabals, I only used those I deemed the most interesting from a RP perspective: The Noose, The Brotherhood, White Putnams, Shadow Chorus, Sanguine Laurel and the Wrens. The others were lesser cabals mostly aligned with the Free Council.</div> </div> </div> </div>I keep the sanguine laurel. And use NPCs from all of the other in different roles. I keep the places of power of the Shadow chorus, the company. And keep the basic deal of the Gravediggers while changing its members. The brotherhood main role i keep but made it the dominant cabal meshing it with the company and making protestas basic motivation intact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T11:50:58-07:00","id":942865,"title":"","content":"I think it's less that they don't care and more that it's infested with Banishers, but hey, whatever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T09:32:04-08:00","id":1003443,"title":"","content":"I've just finished reading the 20 months worth of forum posts I missed while I was away from the game, and even though I still have 3 months to go I thought I would share my experience.<br /> <br /> I absolutely LOVE Boston Unveiled. I don't agree with most of the criticisms that get leveled against it. I ran a highly successful chronicle using a ton of material from this book as well as other 1e source material.<br /> <br /> The loose structure I used was:<br /> <br /> - Gloria Mundi Demo early parts<br /> - Beast of Burden (Boston Unveiled)<br /> - Gloria Mundi Demo middle parts<br /> - Legacy Inductions (Homebrew)<br /> - SAS: The Abedju Cipher<br /> - Gloria Mundi Demo final parts<br /> - SAS: Lines of Power<br /> - Danvers Asylum (Boston Unveiled)<br /> - Mama Desta (Boston Unveiled)<br /> <br /> All of this with the Prince/Secret Concord plotline running in the background.<br /> <br /> I ran 60 sessions in total. The AP can be found right here: <a href=\"http://mage-doomcrew.obsidianportal.com/posts?order_by=oldest&amp;page=1\" target=\"_blank\">http://mage-doomcrew.obsidianportal....=oldest&amp;page=1</a><br /> <br /> It starts a little dry and improves a lot as it progresses.<br /> <br /> PS: I would really appreciate anyone who enjoys it to become a fan for future updates. I'm no DaveB, but I'm pretty proud of the work I put into it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1470,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","user":"Johnny Awesome","date":". 11-16-2016, 11:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T16:50:09-08:00","id":1004707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/942061-your-experiences-running-boston-unveiled?p=1003443#post1003443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...</div> </div> </div> </div>That was a thoroughly enjoyable read, thank you. Could you explain Arachne's legacy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T21:31:02-08:00","id":1008803,"title":"","content":"You can read the Coven of the Summer Ash Legacy right here:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://mage-doomcrew.obsidianportal.com/wikis/coven-of-the-summer-ash-legacy\" target=\"_blank\">http://mage-doomcrew.obsidianportal....mer-ash-legacy</a><br /> <br /> It was created for my game by Obsidian Pharaoh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}